							],
							"documentation": "Scope: one SMSMessage handling behavior, activated after its constructor sets Pending and attemptCount=0. record is a short display name for the existing RecordResult(result) call event; it is bound to that actual operation. success, failure and unknown are exclusive predicates on the received send result. The Success/Failure/Unknown entry actions specify the attemptCount increment in RecordResult, exactly once per result. They do not add a second increment to a separate method body. The Failure self-transition is external, so entry runs again. RecordResult also records status, error and service request metadata. SMSNotificationManager checks CanRetry before each retry; it is true only for Failure and attemptCount<4. The initial send and three retries permit at most four external calls. Final completes this handling behavior without deleting the object or clearing its fields.",
							"regions": [
								{
									"_type": "UMLRegion",
