							"documentation": "Scope: one application screen after ShowApplication initializes existing data. States derive from the existing fields, responses and submission context. No public operation or persistent state member is added. Visible event aliases are bound to existing operations: review=ReviewApplication(); submit and retry=SubmitTravelApplication(). Do activities include the service request, waiting for its result and updating existing response fields. Completion guards are exclusive: ok means review succeeded with unchanged input; failed means the opposite. valid means an accepted unchanged review. saved means confirmed registration. unknown means commit outcome is unresolved. retryable means confirmed non-commit with the review still valid; recheck means confirmed non-commit with an invalid or repriced review. same request requires the same requestKey and reviewed content. when(inputChanged) invalidates the review, while when(closed) completes the screen behavior. Editing entry only invalidates review data; it does not discard product, configuration or traveler input. Unknown submissions preserve the original key and content. SMS failure never undoes a saved application.",
